                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6fd7e60f-efd6-3de7-99d5-4b0bfa056b38",
                        "entry_id": "bd697df3-6e17-36d1-a18a-cf366f260bc8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "физиол. делать (сделать) чувствительным, восприимчивым (к воздействию каких-либо раздражителей и т. п.)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8781ca3-d83f-4061-96b4-f3c377469f26",
                                "sense_id": "6fd7e60f-efd6-3de7-99d5-4b0bfa056b38",
                                "text": "Возможно, что туберкулез подготовляет почву, как бы сенсибилизирует, делает более чувствительными к заболеванию системы элементов, поражаемые при шизофрении."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3f222f6-855e-3e7a-a73e-716afb129c3d",
                        "entry_id": "bd697df3-6e17-36d1-a18a-cf366f260bc8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "фотогр. увеличивать (увеличить) светочувствительности фотоматериалов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "93f9c35c-eb92-421a-bc7a-981c5a827703",
                                "sense_id": "d3f222f6-855e-3e7a-a73e-716afb129c3d",
                                "text": "Значительный процесс в приготовлении фотографических пластинок позволил найти способы сделать фотографическую пластинку чувствительною (сенсибилизировать её) не только для лучей красного света, но и для лучей с ещё большей длиной волны."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a4b32299-8f8c-3a8f-82e8-3d0fe0c65e9c",
                        "entry_id": "bd697df3-6e17-36d1-a18a-cf366f260bc8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "спец. повышать чувствительность к химическим реагентам"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9470d148-a4fe-4b51-807a-41caccde488f",
                                "sense_id": "a4b32299-8f8c-3a8f-82e8-3d0fe0c65e9c",
                                "text": "Потом пластмассу сенсибилизируют, то есть придают ей способность удерживать атомы катализатора."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5c29f11-609e-4021-817b-09fbccf3343a",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd697df3-6e17-36d1-a18a-cf366f260bc8",
                        "target_lang_word": "sensitize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sensitize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6c892ed-46a4-3083-81d2-5869fb5f760e",
                                        "entry_id": "0f7b925a-d782-312d-b286-af22bce831c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (someone or something) sensitive or responsive to certain stimuli."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83fe3fc7-51b3-45c1-9644-122b7bba435c",
                                                "sense_id": "b6c892ed-46a4-3083-81d2-5869fb5f760e",
                                                "text": "Anaphylaxis is the syndrome elicited in a hypersensitive subject upon subsequent exposure to the sensitizing antigen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ee16df3-1aa0-448b-b166-3722ecc157f6",
                                                "sense_id": "b6c892ed-46a4-3083-81d2-5869fb5f760e",
                                                "text": "Great emphasis should be placed on sensitizing the hands to the feel of the water, and the hands should remain sensitized throughout the workout.[…]Swimmers should sensitize the hands at the beginning of every workout by swimming the first 200 meters with their fists tightly clenched."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5c3f536-9209-4000-b6cf-c8c651a4a49e",
                                                "sense_id": "b6c892ed-46a4-3083-81d2-5869fb5f760e",
                                                "text": "BRCA1 sensitizes cells to apoptosis induced by antimicrotubulin agents like taxanes and vinca alkaloids and also abrogates the effect of DNA-damaging agents like cisplatin and etoposide [ 41 ]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bc06547-a164-403f-b7cc-80160bde33a1",
                                                "sense_id": "b6c892ed-46a4-3083-81d2-5869fb5f760e",
                                                "text": "Again, I strongly recommend that you sensitize your collodion-coated plates in a tank, rather than a tray, as it is safer, cleaner, and more process-efficient."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d314454-6414-3a84-8a3d-a1f746015c47",
                                        "entry_id": "0f7b925a-d782-312d-b286-af22bce831c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (someone) increasingly aware of, in a concerned or sensitive way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20669339-f1cd-427e-b477-69c1de41291c",
                                                "sense_id": "7d314454-6414-3a84-8a3d-a1f746015c47",
                                                "text": "Ever since the burglary, we've been more sensitized to home security issues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d01cb8e-3df5-430b-8715-06248053606b",
                                                "sense_id": "7d314454-6414-3a84-8a3d-a1f746015c47",
                                                "text": "At least two stations have been sensitized towards the position gay media professionals […] have to take to protect their job security."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad83668a-69c8-3afb-9eac-a0eb8cf23489",
                                        "entry_id": "0f7b925a-d782-312d-b286-af22bce831c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To render capable of being acted on by actinic rays of light."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
